WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:10.640
So niobium is metal which has a variety of
uses, but it was very good to me in one of

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:18.200
my chemical reactions compounding the niobium
because I had done reactions with vanadium

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.970
which is above niobium in the periodic table
and got one result and then with tantalum

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:30.500
which is below vanadium, no below niobium,
got a different result and then the niobium

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.570
compound gave both results at the same time
and as you varied the temperature it went

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:42.120
either one way or the other. So I have always
regarded niobium as a really friendly element.

